DOCX: a linked section edged by a table is still INCLUDETEXT

0087 wrote a file-linked section as INCLUDETEXT only when its first
and last nodes were paragraphs; any other one fell back, without
notice, to a Word section: the link was lost and section breaks were
added (an .odt linked section opening with a table, saved as DOCX).
0087 papered over the case after a link update by adding empty
paragraphs to the document.
- DOCX export writes every file-linked section as INCLUDETEXT. Where
  the section opens with a table (or a section), a paragraph of its
  own holds the field's start; where it ends with one, a paragraph of
  its own holds the field's end. Reopened, these are the section's
  edge paragraphs, so the next save is the same.
- A cell can't take such a paragraph: a linked section inside a table
  cell, edged by a nested table, is saved as its text, with a warning.
- A link update no longer adds paragraphs beside a table.
- The unreachable RTF branch around INCLUDETEXT's start is gone.

